      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this can simply be\n\n```\nbool ap_power_in_state(enum ap_power_state_mask state_mask)\n{\n    /*\n     * PWRSEQ_DRIVER only exposes stable power states (transitions\n     * occur atomically and are never visible to API consumers), so\n     * these two functions are equivalent.\n     */\n    return ap_power_in_or_transitioning_to_state(state_mask);\n}\n```\n\n`need_mask` is always a subset (possibly empty) of `state_mask` so this is actually just checking whether the result of `ap_power_in_or_transitioning_to_state` is zero. That also means we don\u0027t change the API, which is good (because it\u0027s hard to understand what this new integer mask from `in_or_transitioning_to_state` means).",
      "revId": "7f6c1179855499a6e25043527e9f97619775f356",
